      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Querier is a mid-level Windows box focusing on information disclosure, capturing and cracking Net-NTLMv2 hashes, and weak service permissions. This is a great box for anyone looking to practice their enumeration and Windows priv esc skills. Okay, let&amp;rsquo;s go!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Querier&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/Querier/img/Querier.webp&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://app.hackthebox.com/machines/175&#34;&gt;Hackthebox&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;scanningenumeration&#34;&gt;Scanning/Enumeration&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s kick things off by running a network scan using Nmap. I&amp;rsquo;ll start with a simple scan just to get a feel for what is on this box.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
